HELP(1)                    Funny CLI Manual                     HELP(1)

NAME
    help — Display a list of available commands.

SYNOPSIS
    help

DESCRIPTION
    The 'help' command displays a list of all commands available in the CLI.
    It is useful when you have forgotten a command, discovered a new command,
    or simply have no idea what you are doing.

    Unlike 'man', which explains a specific command in detail, 'help' gives
    you the quick list. Think of it as the table of contents.

USAGE
    > help
        Displays all available commands.

EXAMPLES
    > help
        Shows the complete list of commands supported by the CLI.

FUN FACTS
    - help is usually the first command people try.
    - If you need help using help, try man help.
    - The command list comes directly from the CLI command registry.
    - Knowing what commands exist is generally a good start.

SEE ALSO
    man(1), ls(1), info(1)

AUTHOR
    The Developer Who Wanted You to Smile
